    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0375" n="363" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0010/105: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-05-01">May 1, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1115. American interests—Germany—exchange personnel. Your 1801 and 1802, April
                        29.<anchor n="90" xml:id="d296-f1"/> In view of German insistence upon
                    departure of all German officials on first voyage of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Drottningholm</hi> arrangements are being made to place on board <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Drottningholm</hi> all German officials except those
                    whose present state of health as certified by their own physicians and at their
                    own request may not make their departure advisable at this time.</p>
                <p>The original plan provided that all the German career officials be carried on the
                    first voyage together with certain non-officials whom the Germans had requested.
                    The non-career officials were to follow on next trip of vessel.</p>
                <p>That is now discarded and all officials will be carried on first trip—career and
                    non-career alike.</p>
                <p>These arrangements will necessitate delay from May 5 to May 7 as departure date
                    for ship from New York.</p>
                <p>Please ask Swiss Foreign Office to advise immediately Swiss Minister Berlin for
                    communication to German Foreign Office, if possible by telephone followed by
                    telegraphic confirmation.</p>
                <p>Italian, Hungarian, Rumanian, Japanese and Bulgarian Governments should be
                    informed of delay in sailing of vessel as indicated.</p>
                <p>Inform Morris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
